# Schema and status

Use this `orders` shape. Do not add `clients`, `payments`, or `change_orders` tables.

```
id, token (unique 12-char nanoid), created_at
client_name, client_email, client_phone
brief jsonb  -- type, subjects, detail_level, background, usage, revisions
price_total, price_deposit, price_balance  -- integer piastres
status
deposit_paid_at, balance_paid_at
paymob_deposit_reference, paymob_balance_reference  -- last {token}:{kind}:{attemptId}
paymob_deposit_order_id, paymob_balance_order_id
paymob_deposit_transaction_id, paymob_balance_transaction_id
preview_url, final_url
```

Create the row on brief submit as `awaiting_deposit`, then start checkout. Do not create the order after payment.

## Status machine

```
awaiting_deposit --webhook deposit--> in_progress
in_progress --Nour + preview_url--> ready_for_review
ready_for_review --Nour + final_url--> awaiting_balance
awaiting_balance --webhook balance--> delivered
```

Nour may PATCH only `in_progress → ready_for_review → awaiting_balance`. Reject skips and backwards moves. Dashboard must not write `*_paid_at` or set `in_progress` / `delivered`.

Webhook may only apply deposit (`awaiting_deposit → in_progress`) and balance (`awaiting_balance → delivered`). Failed callbacks do not flip status. If the matching `*_paid_at` is already set, return 200 (idempotent).

`GET` by token must omit `final_url` unless `balance_paid_at` is set. RLS: no browser insert/update; service role on the server only.

Payment rating is computed, not a column: 5 stars if the deposit webhook is within 72 hours of `created_at`, else 4. Alert the client on the brief and `/o/[token]`. Do not block checkout.
